id: doff-bonus
name: Doff Bonus
kind: conditions
maxStacks: 1
# Not a Combat Condition: the rules call it a Doff Bonus and nothing more. A mark, for a bonus
# that has to be held somewhere with a clock on it.
combatCondition: no
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Taken off a piece of Apparel: Combat Rolls higher by its Apparel Bonus until the end of your
  next turn.
text: >
  Doff Bonus: When you remove a piece of Apparel, you may gain a Doff Bonus. A Doff Bonus is a
  boost to your Combat Rolls equal to the Apparel Bonus for that piece of Apparel and lasts until
  the end of your next turn.

  You can only gain a Doff Bonus from each piece of Apparel once per Combat Encounter, and Doff
  Bonuses do not stack. If you would gain a Doff Bonus from multiple pieces of Apparel, only
  apply the largest Doff Bonus.

---

# --- How much, and on what ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Worked out when the piece comes off and kept on the character, `doffBonus`: the piece's Apparel
# Bonus at their base Tier - half as much again, rounded up, for Weights taken off after the 3rd
# Combat Round - on each Combat Roll, or on the one Focal chose alone. See doffBonusFor() in
# module/gear.mjs.
#
# --- How long ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# To the end of their next turn, and a Combat Round longer for each Quality Slot of Segmented
# Weight on the piece - it is always the first time that piece is doffed this Encounter, since
# nothing gives a Doff Bonus twice. A larger one taking its place brings its own clock.

[passive]
strike += doffBonus.strike;
dodge += doffBonus.dodge;
wound += doffBonus.wound;
